---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Stripes from '../../components/Stripes.astro';
import { site, privacyVersion } from '../../data/site';

// La fecha se cambia en src/data/site.ts (privacyVersion), no aquí.
const since = new Date(`${privacyVersion}T12:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
const { legal } = site;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy policy | ${site.name}`}
  description="How BUILDEV handles the personal data it receives through buildev.co: contact form, email, WhatsApp, cookies and products."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <Stripes class="legal-hero__stripes" />
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-hero__date">Effective since {since}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="container legal">
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data we receive through <strong>buildev.co</strong>, what we use it for
        and how you can exercise your rights. It is governed by Ley 1581 de 2012 (Law 1581 of 2012, Colombia's data
        protection law, known as habeas data) and Decreto 1377 de 2013 (compiled in Decreto 1074 de 2015).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Legal name:</strong> {legal.name}</li>
        <li><strong>Tax ID (NIT):</strong> {legal.nit}</li>
        <li><strong>Registered domicile:</strong> {legal.domicile}</li>
        <li><strong>Address:</strong> {legal.address}</li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> {legal.phone}</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email for personal data:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The BUILDEV team handles requests, inquiries and complaints about personal data through that email.</p>

      <h2>2. What data we receive and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, company, email, phone number, the service you are interested in and
          your message. We use it to respond to your request, including sending you any proposal you ask for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email:</strong> if you write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, we receive your
          email address and whatever you tell us. We use it to reply to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>WhatsApp:</strong> if you message us on WhatsApp, we receive your number, your profile name and your
          messages. We use them to reply to you. Meta, which operates WhatsApp, also processes that data under its own
          privacy policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data:</strong> Netlify, which hosts this site, logs data about each visit, such as your IP
          address and browser, to serve and protect the site.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your data or use it to send you advertising.</p>
      <p>
        We do not ask for sensitive data, such as health information, racial or ethnic origin, religious beliefs or
        political views. Please do not include it in your message; if we receive it, we use it only to reply to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is aimed at businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect data from minors; if we receive it, we
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Your authorization</h2>
      <p>
        Before you submit the form, we ask you to authorize this use by checking the corresponding box. We store that
        authorization together with your message, along with the date and the version of this policy you accepted.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your rights</h2>
      <p>As the owner of your data, you can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access, update and correct your data.</li>
        <li>Request proof of the authorization you gave us.</li>
        <li>Find out how we have used it.</li>
        <li>Revoke your authorization or ask us to delete your data, unless a legal or contractual duty requires us to keep it.</li>
        <li>Access it free of charge.</li>
        <li>
          File a complaint with the Superintendencia de Industria y Comercio (SIC, Colombia's data protection authority)
          after first going through the process with us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. How to exercise them</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with your name, your ID, a description of what you are
        requesting, an address or other way to reply to you and, if you wish, any supporting documents.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Inquiries:</strong> we reply within 10 business days. If we cannot meet that deadline, we will tell you
          why and reply within 5 more business days.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Complaints</strong> (correction, update, deletion or non-compliance): we reply within 15 business days.
          If we cannot meet that deadline, we will tell you why and reply within 8 more business days.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a complaint is incomplete, we will ask for what is missing within 5 days. If 2 months go by without a
          response, we will consider the complaint withdrawn.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Where your data is</h2>
      <p>We use these providers, which process data outside Colombia:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify</strong> (United States): hosts this site and stores the form messages on our behalf.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Workspace</strong> (United States and other countries where Google has data centers): provides
          the buildev.co email service, on our behalf.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Meta</strong> (United States and other countries): provides the WhatsApp service.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose data when a competent authority requires it under the law. Our platforms (Rentablo,
        Agendorio and Loyenta) run on other servers and describe their hosting in their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        While we handle your request and, if you hire us, for as long as the business relationship lasts. After that,
        only as long as needed to meet legal obligations or resolve complaints.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        The whole site runs over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) with security headers, and the form filters automated
        submissions. Only authorized BUILDEV staff can access the messages we receive.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not use cookies, analytics tools or ads, and it does not load third-party trackers.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you pick a language with the language selector, we save that choice in your browser's local storage so the
        site opens in that language next time. It is never sent to any server, and you can delete it by clearing this
        site's data in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Our products</h2>
      <p>
        Rentablo, Agendorio and Loyenta have their own privacy policies, which apply when you use those platforms:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Rentablo: <a href="https://rentablo.buildev.co/privacidad" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >rentablo.buildev.co/privacidad</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Agendorio: <a href="https://agendorio.buildev.co/privacidad" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >agendorio.buildev.co/privacidad</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Loyenta: <a href="https://loyenta.buildev.co/privacidad" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >loyenta.buildev.co/privacidad</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="advertising">11. Advertising in our products</h2>
      <p>
        The Rentablo Android app is free and supported by Google AdMob ads. This site, buildev.co, does not show ads.
      </p>
      <p>
        To show those ads, limit how often you see the same one and measure how they perform, Google and its
        advertising partners may use your phone's advertising ID, your IP address and data about how you interact with
        the ads, as described in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Google's advertising policy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        The information you store in the app (for example sales, customers or appointments) is never shared with
        advertisers.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Switzerland or a US state that requires it, we ask
        for your consent or give you the option to opt out before showing ads, using Google's privacy message. You can
        change your choice at any time from the "Ad privacy" option in the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        In any country, you can delete or reset your advertising ID, or opt out of personalized ads, in your phone's
        settings under "Ads". You can also choose whether Google shows you personalized ads in
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My Ad Center</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will publish the new version here with its date. If the change is substantial, for
        example a new data controller or a new purpose, we will announce it on this site before applying it and, if the
        purpose changes, we will ask for your authorization again.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Effective date</h2>
      <p>
        This policy is effective since {since}. Our databases will remain in force while BUILDEV carries on its business
        and the purposes described here still apply.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* El header es transparente arriba: esta franja oscura le da contraste, como el hero de la principal. */
  .legal-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--c-ink-900) 0%, var(--c-ink) 100%);
    color: #fff;
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px));
    padding-bottom: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px);
  }
  .legal-hero :global(.legal-hero__stripes) {
    position: absolute;
    right: -120px;
    bottom: -60px;
    width: min(560px, 80vw);
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.18;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .legal-hero .container {
    position: relative;
  }
  .legal-hero h1 {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }
  .legal-hero__date {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.7);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: calc(68ch + 40px);
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal ul {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .legal li + li {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--c-blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .legal a:hover {
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }
</style>
